{
  "summary": "Microsoft Defender, the built-in antivirus on this computer, has been weakened in several ways at once: real-time protection is off, tamper protection is off, and the entire C: drive is excluded from scanning. Together this means Defender is effectively not protecting the main drive. Look at the Defender findings first and follow the fixes shown in the report. Also confirm you recognize the extra administrator account listed.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "priority": 1,
      "title": "Defender is effectively switched off for the main drive",
      "finding_ids": [
        "DEF-EXCLUSION:c2d1c54c",
        "DEF-REALTIME-OFF:6ed445bc",
        "DEF-TAMPER-OFF:1a04a8d2"
      ],
      "explanation": "These three settings work together. Real-time protection is off, so Defender doesn't check files as they arrive. The whole C: drive, where Windows, your programs and your files normally live, is on Defender's skip list, so even a manual scan would ignore almost everything. Tamper protection is also off, which is what normally stops other programs from changing these settings. Defender's virus definitions are up to date (0 days old), but that doesn't help while it's set up this way. Someone may have changed these settings on purpose, for example while troubleshooting. Malware also commonly makes exactly these changes to hide. Either way, the computer currently has very little antivirus protection. If you didn't make these changes yourself, treat that as a warning sign. Turn protection back on and remove the C: exclusion using the fixes shown in the report for each finding. Once Defender is scanning again, a full scan is a sensible next step."
    },
    {
      "priority": 2,
      "title": "Confirm you recognize the extra administrator account",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291"
      ],
      "explanation": "The account <computer>\\<account-2> has full administrator rights on this computer. Having a separate administrator account is often normal and even good practice, so this is listed as low. However, because Defender's protections have also been turned down, it's worth checking that you or someone you trust created this account. If you don't recognize it, take it seriously and see the fix in the report."
    }
  ],
  "severity_notes": [
    {
      "finding_id": "DEF-TAMPER-OFF:1a04a8d2",
      "suggested_severity": "high",
      "reason": "On its own this would be medium. On this computer, though, tamper protection is off alongside disabled real-time protection and a whole-drive exclusion. That combination suggests the protections may already have been changed, so it deserves the same attention as the other Defender findings."
    }
  ]
}
